toolset.display.name.database=Database
tool.description.list_database_connections=Retrieves a list of configured database connections or data sources in the project.
tool.description.test_database_connection=Checks whether a specific database connection is valid and reachable.
tool.description.create_database_connection=Create a new database connection (data source) by name, DBMS (dbms), JDBC URL (url) and flag to check connection (needToCheckDs). All parameters are required.
tool.description.edit_database_connection=Edit an existing database connection (data source) identified by `connectionId`.
tool.description.list_database_schemas=Retrieves a list of database schemas in the specified database connection.
tool.description.introspect_schema=Introspects a database schema, loading its metadata (tables, columns, indexes, etc.)
tool.description.list_schema_object_kinds=Retrieves supported schema object kinds (e.g., table, view, routine) for the given database connection.
tool.description.list_schema_objects=Retrieves a list of database objects within the given schema.
tool.description.get_database_object_description=Retrieves the structure of a database object (columns, types, keys, indexes) within a particular schema as a hierarchical text representation.
tool.description.list_recent_sql_queries=Retrieves a list of recent (including currently running) queries for the given database connection.
tool.description.cancel_sql_query=Cancels a running query using its unique ID.
tool.description.execute_sql_query=Executes a SQL query against the given database connection.
tool.description.execute_cross_db_query=Executes a cross-database query that reads and joins data from several database connections in one statement.
tool.description.preview_table_data=Previews data of the table, view, materialized view or other table-like object using given database connection.
tool.description.fetch_query_result=Fetches rows from an already executed query by its id, starting at the given row offset.
toolset.database.import.display.name=Database data import
tool.description.inspect_import_file=Reads a data file (CSV/TSV/pipe/semicolon text, JSON, XLS/XLSX, Parquet) and makes it available for import, reporting its columns, a head-of-file sample and any warnings. Does not touch the database.
tool.description.inspect_import_query=Reports the columns and a row sample of a query result the caller already has, and makes it available for import. Does not write.
tool.description.import_data=Imports a previously opened source - a data file or a query result - into an existing table using the column mapping supplied by the caller, after requesting write consent.
